1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:04,109
If you hear a voice on the radio, do not answer yet. Listen first.

2
00:00:04,710 --> 00:00:08,648
The Signal. Part one of four. Static.

3
00:00:09,248 --> 00:00:15,090
A hand-crank radio. No batteries. Thirty turns, ten minutes of power.

4
00:00:15,690 --> 00:00:16,619
It only says static.

5
00:00:16,919 --> 00:00:18,120
Then we listen longer.

6
00:00:20,370 --> 00:00:25,374
One twenty-one point five. Channel nine. The weather band.

7
00:00:25,974 --> 00:00:30,888
...survivors... grid six four... repeating... hold position...

8
00:00:31,488 --> 00:00:32,151
I can answer it!

9
00:00:32,451 --> 00:00:35,744
No. Write the numbers. Listen first.

10
00:00:36,344 --> 00:00:39,380
Why not answer? You do not know who is listening.

11
00:00:40,484 --> 00:00:42,017
A signal works both ways.

12
00:00:43,904 --> 00:00:46,012
Tomorrow, we answer with light.

13
00:00:47,504 --> 00:00:51,605
Part one of four, The Signal. Next: the mirror.
